  <bpmn:collaboration id="L4_03_COLLAB" name="Manage intentional protocol deviations">
    <bpmn:documentation>Model: L4-03
Title: Manage intentional protocol deviations
Parent: L3 A3
Interface: start S1; ends E1, E2, E3; message flows M1, M3, M8
Rule exception: FLW-09 S1 - One business trigger - the investigator's communication of an intentional protocol deviation - arrives as two message types (immediate-hazard report, deviation request). Two start events would break SCP-02 (one entry point per sub-process); splitting L3 step A3 would change the L3 cut confirmed by the user on 06 Nov 2026. Decided by the orchestrator 07 Nov 2026; flagged to the user as revisitable.
Rule exception: ROL-03 P_INV - D1 (orchestrator default, 06 Nov 2026): Investigator/institution is an expanded pool on all levels because investigator obligations are binding steps that must appear as tasks
Rule exception: DEC-06 G1 - XOR split G1: each branch is a distinct business outcome (E1, E2, E3) and ends in its own end event without a join
Rule exception: DEC-06 G6 - XOR split G6: each branch is a distinct business outcome (E2, E3) and ends in its own end event without a join
Rule exception: DEC-06 G7 - XOR split G7: each branch is a distinct business outcome (E4, E5, E6) and ends in its own end event without a join
Rule exception: DEC-06 G8 - XOR split G8: each branch is a distinct business outcome (E5, E6) and ends in its own end event without a join</bpmn:documentation>
