  </bpmn:collaboration>
  <bpmn:process id="L4_03_P_SPON_PROCESS" name="Sponsor" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>One business trigger for the Sponsor process (FLW-09, SCP-02; orchestrator decision V1 round 1, 07 Nov 2026): message start S1 'Intentional protocol deviation communicated' receives both investigator communications (M1 immediate-hazard report, M3 deviation request); task A14 reviews the communication and decides the routing at G1 (FLW-05); it carries the sponsor REQs of the routed paths (REQ-083 immediate hazard, REQ-075 and REQ-076 deviation request), the investigator REQs stay on the investigator elements (V1 round 2); the two paths end in distinct outcomes (DEC-06).
A4 'Handle urgent safety measures' is the interface call activity of C-08 (decided by user 06 Nov 2026; calls null, interface true, S0-18).
Sponsor ends state what the sponsor reaches: E1 'Immediate hazard addressed', E2 'Deviation request approved', E3 'Deviation request rejected'. The l3_cut outcomes 'Immediate-hazard deviation implemented and reported' and 'Intentional deviation approved and implemented' are the investigator ends E4 and E5 (E5 in the glossary form 'Intentional protocol deviation approved and implemented', LBL-04).
The investigator process has one trigger, the l3_cut event 'Intentional protocol deviation considered'; task A8 decides whether the immediate-hazard exception applies (FLW-05), marked [verify] because no source names it as a separate step. Two blank start events were avoided (bpmnlint single-blank-start-event).
C-09: G4 'Deviation from eligibility criteria requested?' leads to the rejection task A6 (M11 S5.1); the FDA-PD24 example stays DRAFT on the request flow (REQ-074).</bpmn:documentation>
